From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT=1: the texture collector waits for the GPU
 at most once a frame to copy GPU-written images back (Fritchii EXP57,
 f93124a6b8); no cap while the pool is short; off by default

Ported from Frizti/Fritchii f93124a6b8 (fritchii-v5.6, GPL-3.0-or-later), "texture_cache: EXP56
skips a cleared depth target's upload; EXP57 caps collector GPU waits", the EXP57 half. Upstream:
a 3 s stall as device memory crossed the expected line, the collector downloading image after
image with runtime.Finish(); EDEN_NX2_EXP57 allows one such wait a frame unless an allocation
failed, the rest wait for later frames ("downloads deferred").

PS5 version. The Vulkan port already batches the collector's copies (headless/
vulkan_gc_downloads.inc: one Finish per batch of up to 64 images / 64 MiB), but nothing caps the
waits per frame: TakePrefetched starts another batch (another Finish) each time the batch runs
out, the Configure(true) pass starts one more, and images the batch cannot take (aliased,
overlapping, MSAA, over the byte budget) still wait one by one (gc_unbatched_drain). On the PS5
these copies run when the pool's largest free block is under 1 GiB (KeepDirtyTextures), which is
the fly-over and new-area case.

EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exactly "1"):
- one collector wait for the GPU a frame: either one batch (port) or one image Cleanup copies
  alone. After it, Cleanup leaves a GPU-written image whose copy is not made yet in place
  (counted as deferred) and the port starts no new batch; copies already made stay usable;
- no cap for the run while wait_exempt is set. The port's half (vulkan_gc_downloads.inc, a front
  change shipped beside this patch) sets it while PoolPressure() is 2 (largest free block under
  EDEN_NX2_TC_POOL_CRITICAL_MIB, 256, or a refusal in the last 120 frames) or any refusal came in
  the last 120 frames (also with EDEN_NX2_TC_POOL_PRESSURE=1), as upstream exempts out_of_memory;
- stderr every 600 frames: "EDEN_GC_ONE_WAIT frame=<n> deferred=<copies left for later>
  waited_frames=<frames with a wait> extra_waits=<waits past the first while exempt>".
Off (unset): WaitHeld() is false and Waited() returns at once; no line. Collector, batches and
the "Texture cache last 600 frames" line as before. Layout only: four u64 in TextureCache.

prepare-vulkan-port.py: every pinned GC anchor still occurs exactly once (checked on the text).
The port replaces the Cleanup capture list with [&, this], so the front's code sees WaitHeld,
Waited and wait_exempt. The front change needs this patch (it names those three); this patch
alone builds and caps only Cleanup's own copies.

Risk: memory. A deferred image keeps its memory a frame or more longer; clean images still go at
the old rate, and the cap lifts at pressure 2. Picture: none (nothing is dropped, only later).

PS5 test: EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT=1 vs the same build without it, same batch, 3 valid runs each,
standard script (house, fly-over 102-117 s, door walk). Watch: fly-over worst frame and frames
over 100 ms, first-visit stutter, EDEN_DEV_GC_DRAIN (batched_calls, unbatched_calls, ns),
EDEN_GC_ONE_WAIT deferred/extra_waits, refusals, pool largest block, out-of-memory crashes.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index cd2d143..4e8b23b 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -194,6 +194,18 @@ constexpr u64 KeepRemadeWindow = 600;
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exact 1; off unless set): Fritchii f93124a6b8 by
+/// Frizti (upstream EDEN_NX2_EXP57). The collector waits for the GPU at most once a frame to copy
+/// GPU-written images back before it deletes them; the images after that wait for a later frame
+/// ("deferred"). One wait is one runtime.Finish(): the Vulkan port's batch of copies
+/// (vulkan_gc_downloads.inc, PrefetchDownloads) or one image Cleanup copies alone. No cap while
+/// the port says the pool is short (RunGarbageCollector's wait_exempt), as upstream lets a failed
+/// allocation through. A stderr line every 600 frames: "EDEN_GC_ONE_WAIT".
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool GcOneWait() {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT");
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 /// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE=1 (off unless set; Fritchii c98e63520a + 07b38b3caf, EXP43=3 of
 /// 1735a6fd13): a render target a clear overwrites whole, which drifted a little off one or more
 /// images of its own single-level, single-layer 2D shape (Ocarina of Time's bump-allocated
@@ -426,8 +438,27 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RunGarbageCollector() {
         // Each pass gets its own scan budget, so the aggressive pass is not starved by earlier ones.
         num_scanned = 0;
     };
+    // EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT (GcOneWait): once this frame's wait for the GPU is spent, a GPU-written
+    // image whose copy is not made yet stays for a later frame. wait_exempt lifts the cap for this
+    // run: the Vulkan port sets it while its PoolPressure() is 2 or the pool refused an allocation
+    // in the last 120 frames (vulkan_gc_downloads.inc). Off: WaitHeld is false, Waited does nothing.
+    bool wait_exempt = false;
+    const auto WaitHeld = [this, &wait_exempt] {
+        return GcOneWait() && !wait_exempt && gc_waited_frame == frame_tick;
+    };
+    const auto Waited = [this] {
+        if (!GcOneWait()) {
+            return;
+        }
+        if (gc_waited_frame == frame_tick) {
+            ++gc_extra_waits; // a second wait this frame: the cap was lifted
+        } else {
+            gc_waited_frame = frame_tick;
+            ++gc_waited_frames;
+        }
+    };
     const auto Cleanup = [this, &num_iterations, &num_scanned, &high_priority_mode, &aggressive_mode,
-                          &evict_old_costly](ImageId image_id) {
+                          &evict_old_costly, &WaitHeld, &Waited](ImageId image_id) {
         if (num_iterations == 0 || (count_evictions && num_scanned >= 8192)) {
             return true;
         }
@@ -466,12 +497,18 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RunGarbageCollector() {
             return false;
         }
         if (must_download) {
+            // EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT: this frame's wait is spent; the image stays, nothing is lost.
+            if (WaitHeld()) {
+                ++gc_downloads_deferred;
+                return false;
+            }
             auto map = runtime.DownloadStagingBuffer(image.unswizzled_size_bytes);
             const auto copies = FullDownloadCopies(image.info);
             image.DownloadMemory(map, copies);
             runtime.Finish();
             SwizzleImage(*gpu_memory, image.gpu_addr, image.info, copies, map.mapped_span, swizzle_data_buffer);
             ++gc_download_deletes;
+            Waited();
         }
         // EDEN_UP_NO_STALE_UPLOAD. Kept apart from the download above: the Vulkan port
         // (prepare-vulkan-port.py) also writes such an image back from a prefetched copy.
@@ -1522,6 +1559,19 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
                  churn[Churn::StagingBytes] >> 20, churn[Churn::DeviceAllocations],
                  churn[Churn::DeviceFrees], churn[Churn::DescriptorPools], slot_images.size());
     }
+    if (GcOneWait() && frame_tick % 600 == 0) {
+        // EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT, the last 600 frames: deferred = copies left for a later frame;
+        // waited_frames = frames with a collector wait for the GPU; extra_waits = waits past the
+        // first while the pool was short (no cap then).
+        std::fprintf(stderr,
+                     "EDEN_GC_ONE_WAIT frame=%llu deferred=%llu waited_frames=%llu "
+                     "extra_waits=%llu\n",
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(frame_tick),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(gc_downloads_deferred),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(gc_waited_frames),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(gc_extra_waits));
+        gc_downloads_deferred = gc_waited_frames = gc_extra_waits = 0;
+    }
     if (RefusalEvictEnabled()) {
         // EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT=1: a refusal anywhere since the last frame's end (an image here,
         // or the allocator: staging and other buffers, decode images, an image placed in host
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index e6055b0..07a0e9c 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -188,6 +188,10 @@ class TextureCache : public VideoCommon::ChannelSetupCaches<TextureCacheChannelI
     u64 gc_deletes{};
     u64 gc_costly_deletes{};
     u64 gc_download_deletes{}; ///< Evictions that downloaded the image first (a full GPU wait)
+    u64 gc_downloads_deferred{}; ///< EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT: copies left for a later frame
+    u64 gc_waited_frames{};      ///< EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT: frames with a collector wait
+    u64 gc_extra_waits{};        ///< EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT: waits past the first (pool short)
+    u64 gc_waited_frame{~0ULL};  ///< EDEN_UP_GC_ONE_WAIT: the frame of the collector's last wait
     u64 async_decodes_queued{};
     u64 images_created{};
     u64 area_images_created{};  ///< Images created since the start (AreaEvict; never reset)
-- 
2.47.0
